   "text": {
    "L1": "Reflection is the bouncing back of light from a surface.",
    "L2": "A smooth, shiny surface, such as a plane mirror, can form a clear image.",
    "L3": "The image is not on the mirror surface. It appears behind the mirror, as far behind as the object is in front.",
    "L4": "A plane mirror image is upright and the same size as the object.",
    "L5": "A mirror swaps left and right. This is called lateral inversion, not an upside-down flip.",
    "L6": "If a ray strikes at 30 degrees to the normal, it reflects at 30 degrees on the other side.",
    "L7": "So a clear plane-mirror image is upright, the same size, behind the mirror, and laterally inverted.",
    "L8": "Tap the three true features of a plane-mirror image."
   },
